 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.

+## Filtering
+
+The view has a filter bar: free text over the name, and a set of statuses. Both
+are applied by the backend — `findAll` and `count` both take a `CustomerFilter`
+— so a filtered grid is still one page of rows and one count query.
+
+The name filter is split on whitespace into terms, every one of which must occur
+in the first or the last name; matching ignores case and accents, so `makinen`
+finds `Mäkinen`. The name field reports lazily, once the typing pauses, so a name
+costs a query or two rather than one per keystroke.
+
+The filter is in the URL as `?name=…&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`, written with
+`replaceState` so that typing does not fill up the back button. Opening such a
+URL applies the filter and fills in both fields.
+
